<second_data>
The error you're encountering is due to the fact that you're trying to use a server component (`page`) as a client component. In Next.js, you can't use async/await directly in a page component like you would in a regular React component. Instead, you should use `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps` to fetch data on the server-side and pass it to your component as props.

Here's how you can refactor your code to fix the issue:

```jsx
"use client";

import React, { useState } from "react";
import { updateOrder } from "@/app/BookAPI";
import Link from "next/link";
import { useRouter } from "next/router";

const UpdateOrderPage = ({ id, initialCustomerName }) => {
  const [customerName, setCustomerName] = useState(initialCustomerName);
  const router = useRouter();

  const handleSubmit = async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    try {
      const orderStatus = await updateOrder(id, customerName);
      console.log(orderStatus);
      router.push("/"); // Redirect to homepage or any other page after successful update
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("Error updating order:", error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <div>
        <h1>Update Order</h1>
      </div>
      <div>
        <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
          <label>
            Customer Name
            <input
              type="text"
              value={customerName}
              onChange={(e) => setCustomerName(e.target.value)}
            />
          </label>
          <button type="submit">Update Order</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

export async function getServerSideProps({ params }) {
  const { id } = params;

  // Fetch initial customer name or any other data you need from your API
  const res = await fetch(`https://your-api-url.com/orders/${id}`);
  const orderData = await res.json();
  const initialCustomerName = orderData.customerName || "";

  return {
    props: {
      id,
      initialCustomerName,
    },
  };
}

export default UpdateOrderPage;
```

In this refactored version, I've created a new component `UpdateOrderPage` that accepts `id` and `initialCustomerName` as props. The `getServerSideProps` method is used to fetch the initial customer name from your API and pass it as a prop to the component. The `useRouter` hook is used to handle redirection after successfully updating the order.
</second_data>

