```php
function saveGravatar($size, $email) {
    // Generate Gravatar URL
    $gravatarUrl = 'https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/' . md5(strtolower(trim($email))) . '?s=' . $size;

    // Initialize cURL
    $ch = curl_init($gravatarUrl);

    // Set cURL options
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_HEADER, true);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_NOBODY, true);
    curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION, true);

    // Execute cURL and get response info
    curl_exec($ch);
    $responseInfo = curl_getinfo($ch);

    // Close cURL
    curl_close($ch);

    // If the HTTP response code is 200, the image exists
    if ($responseInfo['http_code'] == 200) {
        // Generate a unique filename for the image
        $filename = md5($email) . '.jpg';

        // Save the image to the current directory
        file_put_contents($filename, file_get_contents($gravatarUrl));

        return $filename;
    } else {
        return false;
    }
}
```

This function will return the filename of the saved image if the Gravatar exists, or false if it does not. The image will be saved in the same directory as the script. You may want to modify this to save the image to a different location, or to handle errors differently.

Also, please note that this function does not check if the email address is valid. You may want to add additional error checking to ensure that the email address is in the correct format.

